items.text:
I actually think your routine looks good enough, the order looks fine too. Sounds like it's working well for you too. Personally I might want less actives in the morning, and switch the BHA to PM routine and alternate with glycolic toner. But then again your skin is improving with this routine, a switch isn't necessary.

&amp;#x200B;

I'm not familiar with CCs and in-grown hairs, but perhaps you can slightly increase your TO peeling solution and aztec clay mask usage if you think your skin can tolerate it.

I just had a mini haul recently and I have so many products that I still haven't even opened, and some others that I'm trying out to see if my skin likes them. But there's always so many sales and promotions going on and they really challenge my self-control, especially when I see products I've been tempted to try go on sale.

&amp;#x200B;

So what I'm doing is listing down all the products I already own, and roughly plan a schedule to try out my newer products for 2 weeks (or more, it's sometimes hard to tell if my skin hates something or is just breaking out). It helps me control my shopping impulses and see if something I'm considering to buy is really needed.
